WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.444
This is a web browser running entirely inside Cloudflare Workers.

00:00:04.444 --> 00:00:06.041
No Chrome, no container.

00:00:06.421 --> 00:00:07.611
It is called Kitesurf.

00:00:07.611 --> 00:00:11.180
Cloudflare built it for agents, and this week it went open source.

00:00:13.582 --> 00:00:14.415
Hi, I'm Skerry!

00:00:14.415 --> 00:00:17.747
I read Kitesurf's code to see which parts of a browser it

00:00:17.747 --> 00:00:19.691
kept, and what one page really costs.

00:00:21.558 --> 00:00:24.703
A browser does the same work in the same order.

00:00:24.703 --> 00:00:25.647
First it fetches.

00:00:25.647 --> 00:00:28.163
In Kitesurf one gateway Worker does every fetch.

00:00:28.563 --> 00:00:32.754
Then it parses HTML into a DOM, here Rust compiled to WebAssembly,

00:00:32.754 --> 00:00:35.199
in a fresh isolate for every page.

00:00:35.599 --> 00:00:37.522
Then the page's own JavaScript runs.

00:00:37.522 --> 00:00:38.484
Hold that thought.

00:00:38.884 --> 00:00:41.740
Then style and layout, with Servo's CSS engine.

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:44.953
The page isolate also records the scene to draw.

00:00:45.353 --> 00:00:50.546
For a screenshot, a second isolate replays that scene into pixels on the CPU.

00:00:50.546 --> 00:00:52.029
Real pixels, no GPU.

00:00:52.029 --> 00:00:54.255
For plain text, it never starts.

00:00:54.655 --> 00:00:58.681
Last, it encodes a PNG or JPEG, or writes a vector PDF.

00:01:00.242 --> 00:01:01.275
Cloudflare's own diagram.

00:01:01.275 --> 00:01:05.062
The engine is the only part that keeps state, and only

00:01:05.062 --> 00:01:06.439
for one WebSocket session.

00:01:06.819 --> 00:01:10.321
Every frame is a call to the renderer, which pulls the scene

00:01:10.321 --> 00:01:11.780
and sends back JPEG bytes.

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:15.282
It holds nothing, so it can be killed and reloaded any time.

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:20.784
Workers forbid eval, so a browser cannot just hand page code

00:01:20.784 --> 00:01:22.087
to V8 at runtime.

00:01:22.087 --> 00:01:24.042
Kitesurf splits the scripts in two.

00:01:24.462 --> 00:01:28.694
Scripts it finds in the HTML, it fetches and bakes into the

00:01:28.694 --> 00:01:31.516
code the page's Dynamic Worker is created from.

00:01:31.516 --> 00:01:32.926
V8 runs those natively.

00:01:33.346 --> 00:01:37.381
A script the page inserts later cannot be baked in time.

00:01:37.381 --> 00:01:41.049
It runs on Boa, a JavaScript interpreter compiled to WebAssembly.

00:01:41.469 --> 00:01:44.438
So does anything an agent sends over CDP.

00:01:44.438 --> 00:01:48.149
Every page dot evaluate from Puppeteer runs on the interpreter.

00:01:48.569 --> 00:01:51.697
On the next page of the same session, the chunks it learned

00:01:51.697 --> 00:01:53.521
are baked too, and V8 takes over.

00:01:55.325 --> 00:01:58.671
Because the renderer only reads a scene, it can live somewhere else.

00:01:59.051 --> 00:02:00.848
Here it runs in a terminal.

00:02:00.848 --> 00:02:02.645
The page still executes on Cloudflare.

00:02:04.308 --> 00:02:08.611
To work with Puppeteer and Playwright, it speaks the Chrome DevTools Protocol.

00:02:08.611 --> 00:02:11.121
The version it pins has fifty-eight domains.

00:02:11.541 --> 00:02:15.182
Fifteen are routed, with a hundred and eleven methods handled.

00:02:15.182 --> 00:02:18.095
Thirty answer every call with an empty success.

00:02:18.095 --> 00:02:19.552
Thirteen say not found.

00:02:21.867 --> 00:02:23.934
For most agent work that is enough.

00:02:23.934 --> 00:02:26.887
Here an agent lists a page's WebMCP tools through it.

00:02:27.267 --> 00:02:29.211
But the empty success is the trap.

00:02:29.211 --> 00:02:32.267
A script that sets a time zone is told it worked.

00:02:33.550 --> 00:02:37.375
Cloudflare's benchmark says the design pays off in memory and CPU

00:02:37.375 --> 00:02:38.765
on the median page.

00:02:38.765 --> 00:02:43.285
It loses on wall time, and heavy news pages flip the CPU win.

00:02:44.942 --> 00:02:46.066
Here is the formula.

00:02:46.942 --> 00:02:48.631
But nobody bills that memory.

00:02:48.631 --> 00:02:52.686
Host it yourself and each screenshot loads at least two Dynamic Workers.

00:02:53.106 --> 00:02:55.499
The price list charges for every one created.

00:02:56.152 --> 00:02:58.282
So the creation fee is the bill.

00:02:58.282 --> 00:03:01.934
At ten thousand screenshots a day, about twelve hundred dollars a month.

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:04.964
And yes, it runs Doom.

00:03:07.517 --> 00:03:10.020
Kitesurf is a real browser built from isolates.

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:13.462
Cheap for Cloudflare to run, free in beta, and not yet

00:03:13.462 --> 00:03:14.714
cheap to host yourself.

00:03:16.442 --> 00:03:18.978
Baked scripts on V8, the rest on Boa.

00:03:18.978 --> 00:03:19.928
A partial protocol.

00:03:19.928 --> 00:03:21.830
And a bill set by isolates.

00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:22.781
Thanks for watching!

00:03:23.201 --> 00:03:25.301
Every source is in the full article.

00:03:25.301 --> 00:03:25.901
I'm Skerry.

00:03:25.901 --> 00:03:26.202
Bye!
